      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8e34f715-c946-5a4c-8570-1d8b7d1f804b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michał Wiśniowiecki, Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki, Michael I\n- Places: Wiśniowiec\n- Roles: szlachcic, prince, magnate, King of Poland, Grand Duke of Lithuania\n- Organizations: Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth\n\nFacts:\n- Michał Wiśniowiecki was a Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth szlachcic, prince at Wiśniowiec, and magnate.\n- Michał Wiśniowiecki died in 1616.\n- Michał Wiśniowiecki was the grandfather of future Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth monarch Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki.\n- Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki, also known as Michael I, was born on May 31, 1640.\n- Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki ruled the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth as King of Poland and Grand Duke of Lithuania from September 29, 1669 until his death.\n- Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki died on November 10, 1673.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "419bb8d9-237e-5f00-8543-5de182fac000",
        "text": "Page: Michał Wiśniowiecki. Sentence: Michał Wiśniowiecki (died 1616) was a Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth szlachcic, prince at Wiśniowiec, magnate, grandfather of future Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth monarch, Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki.\nPage: Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki. Sentence: Michael I (Polish: \"Michał Korybut Wiśniowiecki\" , Lithuanian: \"Mykolas I Kaributas Višnioveckis\" ; May 31, 1640 – November 10, 1673) was the ruler of the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth as King of Poland and Grand Duke of Lithuania from September 29, 1669 until his death in 1673.",
